      "customData": {
        "section": "1-what",
        "anchor": [
          0,
          1340,
          "lt"
        ]
      },
      "text": "A trained model is a file of weights. Inference is running it to answer requests, and inference engineering is\neverything between a request and its tokens: which requests run together, where their state lives in memory,\nand how each step uses the hardware, so that many people are served fast and at a low cost per token.",
      "originalText": "A trained model is a file of weights. Inference is running it to answer requests, and inference engineering is\neverything between a request and its tokens: which requests run together, where their state lives in memory,\nand how each step uses the hardware, so that many people are served fast and at a low cost per token.",
      "fontSize": 30,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "aT"
